   "subject": "multidimensional ordinal IRT with different response options/response scales",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Is it possible to run an IRT model and fit a single latent variable to items with different numbers of response options? eg, a unidimensional IRT model with item one having 4 response options, and items two and three with 3 response options. Thanks!</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tAvrLiScAgAJ",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2020-04-23T17:12:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: multidimensional ordinal IRT with different response options/response scales",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, see the documentation of the &#39;itemtype&#39; input for precisely this, and note that the number of unique category information per item is automatically managed by the package.<div> <br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
